From c1478f911326859fccf7182fdcf99495eaf58b81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 22:39:47 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] wip/host-expert-tier: -lme is a per-TENSOR pinned-master
 budget, filled in descending hotness

The transport is settled (hipHostMalloc everywhere; `pinned` is the fastest at
every device count: 645.9/1105.4 prefill and 53.5/72.0 decode at 1/2 devices), but
a pinned host master is a SECOND COPY of the host expert bytes.  `-lme` sized a
pool, so the one thing a user wanted to cap -- the non-swappable footprint -- was
not capped at all, and the mode distinction (`pinned` vs `pool`) keyed the whole
staging branch on where the master lives rather than on the budget.

This makes `-lme` the budget, resolved at MODEL LOAD, before any host expert
tensor is placed:

  --host-experts pinned : the whole set (unchanged meaning)
  -lme auto (default)   : the whole set when it fits MOE_HOST_LIMIT_FRAC (80%) of
                          MemAvailable; otherwise NO pinned master -- every host
                          expert stays in the read-only model mapping and the
                          bounded pinned pool serves the reads (the not-fitting
                          band, unchanged from `--host-experts pool`)
  -lme N                : N GiB, spent on WHOLE tensors in DESCENDING HOTNESS (the
                          persisted heat prior ranks them, so the bytes that are
                          actually read are the ones that are pinned); the rest
                          stays in the model mapping

Why whole tensors and not a per-expert region: a pinned master is addressed by
expert index (stride nb[2]), so a partial one needs holes plus a changed cold-read
encoding (the `id - n_res_slots -> slot` encoding is shared with the KV/arena
paths).  With whole tensors a pinned tensor IS today's `pinned` master, so its
table keeps the single-launch staging branch, the in-place cold read and the UVA
alias, and `host_pinned` becomes a per-TABLE truth about the weights.  Per-expert
residency inside a table stays the pool's job.

Plumbing: a metadata pre-pass over the GGUF index (`weights_map`) computes the
host expert byte total and the candidate set the `-ncmoe` tail/explicit override
rule will host, so the budget is decidable before the arch creates a tensor; the
heat prior is opened early through two new device-API entries
(`ggml_backend_dev_moe_heat_open/_score`) instead of being loaded at the first
tensor's DATA copy (long after placement); `llama_host_experts_mode_apply`'s pool
enable re-resolves `g_pool_enabled`, because the loader's decision can arrive
after `parse_env()`.

Census, always at INFO, plus the per-tensor tier accounting.

Measured on Qwen3.6-35B-A3B Q4_K_M, -ncmoe 40, 2 devices (0,2), -n 300, prose 5246:

  arm                     prefill   decode   pinned/pageable (MiB)   text
  -lme auto (fits)         1105.4    71.9     18662 / 0               sh=231512fc77e5
  -lme 64 (clamped)        1106.0    71.7     18662 / 0               sh=231512fc77e5
  -lme 8                    505.1    50.1      8064 / 10598           sh=231512fc77e5
  auto, set does NOT fit    713.7    51.8         0 / 18662           sh=231512fc77e5

1 device: auto 645.2/53.4 (sh=4ae33f7bd65c), -lme 8 447.1/48.4 (same text).
Byte-identical text in every pair; check-gpu-faults clean on every arm.
